<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandar Lengeh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lingeh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandar Lengeh is a port on the Iranian coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>, in Hormozgan province. In the 18th and 19th centuries it was ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> and thrived on pearling and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepot</a> trade. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> took direct control in 1887 and imposed new customs duties from 1902, many of its merchants moved to Dubai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bandar-lengeh.jpg" alt="Bandar Lengeh" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hasanbardal · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BandarLengeh-Beach-4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
